  "title": "Two kinds of interface in the knot's spaces",
  "subject": "How the parts of a knot's space (a cubic system on which not-all-equal fails) meet across small cuts",
  "conclusion": "Across every nontrivial 2-edge cut of a knot's space one side accepts exactly equality and the other exactly disequality (complementary two-place parity, no hub), and across every nontrivial 3-edge cut the point side accepts exactly an antipodal pair and the line side its complement (a knot against a hub, up to signs). This corrects KNOT-COMPOSE-20261101-001-D001: the knot's spaces do not compose only through hubs.",
  "authority_class": "proof",
